{
  "id": "Compound::DB06738 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Ketobemidone appears to interact with Cyp2c19 through a series of molecular and enzymatic pathways, as evidenced by its binding to Cyp2c9 and subsequent participation in limonene monooxygenase activity. The evidence suggests that Ketobemidone may modulate Cyp2c19's function by influencing the activity of Cyp2c9, which in turn affects the enzymatic activity of Cyp2c19. The presence of multiple pathways—such as the participation of Cyp2c9 in (r)-limonene 6-monooxygenase and (s)-limonene 7-monooxygenase activities—indicates that Ketobemidone may influence the specificity or efficiency of Cyp2c19 in metabolizing different substrates. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Ketobemidone affects Cyp2c19 remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp2c9 as a critical mediator in the interaction between Ketobemidone and Cyp2c19, emphasizing the importance of enzyme activity in drug metabolism.",
